From: omacut-windows prepare-source <prepare-source@omacut-windows.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:57:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Let go of a replaced dialog button's letter at once

The quit question's buttons depend on whether an export is running, so
when an export ends the Repeater replaces them. On Qt 6.8 the replaced
buttons are destroyed but only freed on a later turn of the event loop,
and until then their mnemonic Shortcut stays registered and enabled. The
old Quit button's Q and the window's own Q are then ambiguous, so a Q
pressed right after an export finishes quits nothing.

Clear the Shortcut's sequences when the button is destroyed, which takes
them out of the shortcut map straight away.

qmlQuitAsksWhileExporting fails without this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/DialogButton.qml | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/DialogButton.qml b/src/DialogButton.qml
index 9ff85962a22d779237dc9ce4cb29e2c8130b205e..dd0425cf95db8089a2196eabe92ca41c68c87d0b 100644
--- a/src/DialogButton.qml
+++ b/src/DialogButton.qml
@@ -45,7 +45,13 @@ Button {
             : control.primary ? Qt.darker(theme.accent, 1.15) : "#3a3a3e"
     }
     HoverHandler { cursorShape: Qt.PointingHandCursor }
+    // A button the Repeater replaces (the quit question's buttons change with
+    // the export) is destroyed, but on Qt 6.8 it is freed, and its letter
+    // let go, only on a later turn of the event loop. Until then the old Quit
+    // button's Q makes the window's own Q ambiguous, and neither fires.
+    Component.onDestruction: mnemonicShortcut.sequences = []
     Shortcut {
+        id: mnemonicShortcut
         sequences: [control.mnemonic, "Alt+" + control.mnemonic]
         enabled: control.visible && control.mnemonic !== ""
         context: Qt.ApplicationShortcut
